---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config";
---

<Base title="Privacy — Apptivate" description="Privacy notice for Apptivate Limited.">
  <Nav />
  <main class="section">
    <div class="container legal">
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 22 October 2026</p>

      <p>
        This notice explains how {siteConfig.legalName} (“Apptivate”, “we”, “us”) handles personal data
        when you use <a href={siteConfig.canonical}>apptivate.uk</a>, email us, send the contact form, or
        book a call. It is written for a small UK company. It is not legal advice.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        The data controller is {siteConfig.legalName}, company number {siteConfig.companyNumber},
        registered in England and Wales. Registered office: {siteConfig.registeredOffice}.
      </p>
      <p>
        Contact: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>We only collect what we need to reply and, if we work together, to deliver the work:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact form:</strong> name, email, company (if you give it), message, and the consent
          tick. The form is processed by Formspree.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email:</strong> whatever you send to {siteConfig.contactEmail}, including any attachments.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Booking:</strong> if you use Calendly, they collect your name, email and meeting details
          so we can hold the call. That happens on Calendly’s site under their terms.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting logs:</strong> this site is a static site on GitHub Pages. The host may log
          technical data such as IP address, browser type and pages requested, for security and to serve
          the site.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not run advertising or analytics tags on this website. We do not buy marketing lists or
        sell your details.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          To answer an enquiry or book a call — legitimate interests, and consent where you tick the form
          box (UK GDPR Articles 6(1)(f) and 6(1)(a)).
        </li>
        <li>
          To provide services, invoicing and support if you become a client — contract (Article 6(1)(b)).
        </li>
        <li>
          To keep records we are required to keep — legal obligation (Article 6(1)(c)).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We share personal data only as needed to run the business. Typical recipients:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Formspree, for the contact form</li>
        <li>Calendly, if you book a call through their link</li>
        <li>GitHub, which hosts this website</li>
        <li>Our email and office providers</li>
        <li>
          Our delivery team in Chennai, India, where we need them to quote or do the work, acting on our
          instructions
        </li>
        <li>Professional advisers, insurers, or authorities if the law requires it</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Some of those organisations are outside the UK. Where that happens, we rely on an adequacy
        decision or other safeguards they publish (for example standard contractual clauses).
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiry and booking details are kept only as long as we need them to respond and follow up —
        usually up to 24 months if we do not start work, unless you ask us to delete them sooner. If you
        become a client, we keep records for the life of the engagement and for a reasonable period
        afterwards (typically up to six years) for tax, accounting and legal reasons.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK GDPR you can ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access the personal data we hold about you</li>
        <li>correct it if it is wrong</li>
        <li>erase it, or restrict or object to how we use it</li>
        <li>receive a copy in a portable format, where that right applies</li>
        <li>withdraw consent, where we rely on consent — that does not affect use before you withdraw</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>. You also have
        the right to complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office at
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reputable providers and restrict access to people who need it. No website or email system
        is completely secure; please do not send passwords or payment card numbers through the contact
        form.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        See our <a href="/cookies/">cookie notice</a>. This site does not use non-essential cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this notice from time to time. The date at the top is the latest version. If we
        make a material change, we will update this page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
